osition (acting last post-flop) and potentially good pot odds to just call (0), the playability of this hand is poor. Playing it often leads to difficult situations where you bleed more chips. Since you are currently behind in the overall game score (-2500), it is crucial to preserve your chips for hands with higher equity rather than gambling on the lowest suited connectors. The most disciplined and +EV (Expected Value) move here is to fold and wait for a better spot.\n\nAnswer: -1'}
